<title>FRANCE: French consumer prices flat to 0.1 pct up in April.</title>
<headline>French consumer prices flat to 0.1 pct up in April.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following provisional data:</p>
<p>				    Apr	  Mar     Apr 1996</p>
<p> Month-on-month inflation  0.0/0.1     0.1	  0.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year inflation    0.9/1.0     1.1	  2.4</p>
<p> CPI Index (base 1990)  115.0/115.1   115.0	 114.0</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following breakdown of the consumer price index for all households in mainland France, base 1990.</p>
<p>     Category		  Weight(pct) index  1-mo   3-mo  yr/yr</p>
<p> Food excluding tobacco	 20.20    108.0   0.2   -1.0    0.5</p>
<p> Private-sector manufactures  32.77    108.9  -0.1    1.4    0.0</p>
<p> Private-sector services	19.64    126.3   0.2    0.5    1.7</p>
<p> Energy				8.66    113.9  -0.9   -1.6    2.1</p>
<p> Public services ex energy     6.46    131.0   0.3    1.2    2.9</p>
<p> Rent, water			 6.68    130.5   0.1    0.5    1.7</p>
<p> Health spending		   5.59    110.2   0.2    0.1    0.5</p>
<p> Total excluding tobacco	98.02    113.9   0.0    0.3    0.8</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
